sloppy in its definitions. That definition is so broad as to be useless.
It would include a writer's decision not to publish his own work; a writer
losing his work by accident and thus being unable to publish it; a
publisher rejecting a work because there isn't space or because it's in
the wrong category; and lack of money preventing a publishing project from
getting off the ground.

