>is what alt.censorship would be about under that definition?

Dictionaries, being very general guides to word usage, are not terribly
useful for a philosophical discussion.  The preparers of most ordinary
dictionaries claim to describe word usage in a summary way rather than
to prescribe an appropriate use of any word.  If you already know and
use a word, chances are that you have already "customized" it to fit the 
area of discussion within which you wish to use it.  Dictionary definitions
are usually neither precise or profound.  Writers are; and when many writers
use a word in perhaps slightly different ways, the lexicographer takes this
fact along with the history of the word's usage to give a very approximate
"ballpark" description of such usage.  Otherwise, our dictionaries would be
much larger and would deal more with concepts than words.  Indeed, it would
likely be more appropriate to call them "encyclopaedias of concepts" instead
of "dictionaries".

Steve Nichols


